: [18031, 56431], "confidence": 0.78, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_22", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_21", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "No directed, time-respecting chain from 1006 to 1860 is supported by the temporal evidence. There is no direct 1006->1860 interaction (step_02), and 1006 has no observed directed contact to 153 (step_22). While 1006 does contact node 45 (step_08) and 153 does contact 1860 (step_10), the 45\u2013153 interaction is oriented 153->45 (step_09), not 45->153, so the sequence cannot carry influence 1006 -> ... -> 153 -> 1860. Other 1006 neighbors show no interactions to 1860 (steps_12,14), and although both nodes (and intermediary 153) are active (steps_01,21,06) and connected in the static/k-hop view (step_03), those confounders do not provide the necessary directed, temporally ordered links within \u2264600 time units to support a cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_68f9c03d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.78,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No directed, time-respecting chain from 1006 to 1860 is supported by the temporal evidence. There is no direct 1006->1860 interaction (step_02), and 1006 has no observed directed contact to 153 (step_22). While 1006 does contact node 45 (step_08) and 153 does contact 1860 (step_10), the 45\u2013153 interaction is oriented 153->45 (step_09), not 45->153, so the sequence cannot carry influence 1006 -> ... -> 153 -> 1860. Other 1006 neighbors show no interactions to 1860 (steps_12,14), and although both nodes (and intermediary 153) are active (steps_01,21,06) and connected in the static/k-hop view (step_03), those confounders do not provide the necessary directed, temporally ordered links within \u2264600 time units to support a cascade.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 223340, "total_output_tokens": 11808, "total_tokens": 235148, "total_latency_ms": 188865, "llm_calls": 32, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}